      "message": "I finally found the place where the WKEN bit is set: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/chip/npcx/lpc.c#1106\n\nI believe we need to check for CONFIG_ESPI there and decide not to enable the wake source in that case. But let\u0027s wait for confirmation from Nuvoton.\n\ndiff --git a/chip/npcx/lpc.c b/chip/npcx/lpc.c\nindex e8b59f12d..328a5bbc1 100644\n--- a/chip/npcx/lpc.c\n+++ b/chip/npcx/lpc.c\n@@ -1103,9 +1103,11 @@ static void lpc_init(void)\n        CLEAR_BIT(NPCX_WKMOD(MIWU_TABLE_0, MIWU_GROUP_5), 7);\n        /* Handle interrupting on any edge */\n        SET_BIT(NPCX_WKAEDG(MIWU_TABLE_0, MIWU_GROUP_5), 7);\n+#ifndef CONFIG_ESPI\n        /* Enable wake-up input sources */\n        SET_BIT(NPCX_WKEN(MIWU_TABLE_0, MIWU_GROUP_5), 7);\n #endif\n+#endif\n }",
